### Page 5 of 17

```text
UDC-21-00046

March 1, 2021
ANALYSIS OF APPLICATION CONFORMANCE WITH REVIEW CRITERIA:

Should the Planning Commission wish to recommend approval of the Zoning Map Amendment, the
Commission must make the following findings required in UDC 2.2.1.d a detailed analysis is below:

1) The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan.  (UDC 2.2.1.d.1)

The future land use designation for the subject property is Urban Residential. This future land
use designation was updated with the Connect 2045 Transportation Master Plan. The most
appropriate zone for the Urban Residential designation is LR, MR, HR, NR-1, NR-2, and NR-3. The
zoning map amendment fulfills the following development policies and physical patterns in the
Comprehensive Plan:

•
Policy 1.4.A. Infill Opportunities: The zoning map amendment will facilitate the use of
an existing lot for new development and provide an infill opportunity. The zone change
and annexation will bring the lot into the City and permit access to the Mission Village
project.
•
Policy 1.2.C: County Enclave: The annexation and zoning map amendment will remove a
county enclave from within City limits.

Through the policies addressed in PlanCheyenne, the proposed zone change for the subject
property from County MR to MR complies with review criteria 1.

2) The application is compatible with nearby property, specifically considering existing zoning,
the Comprehensive Plan, and any other official plans and policies created under the guidance
of that plan for these areas; (UDC 2.2.1.d.2)

The application is compatible with nearby property zoning and future land use designations. The
subject property is situated within an Urban Residential neighborhood that is zoned MR. The
proposed zone change simply requests changing the zoning designation for the property from
County MR to City MR.

The proposed zone change for the subject property from County MR to MR complies with
review criteria 2.

3) The suitability of the subject property for development according to the standards and uses of
the existing zoning district, compared to the suitability of the subject property for
development according to the standards and uses of the proposed zoning district (UDC
2.2.1.d.3)

The existing lot is proposed to be used for access to the Mission Village housing development.
The subject property is surrounded by MR zoning and is being used as access for a property that
is zoned MR, leading to the MR zone being the most suitable district for the subject property.

The proposed zone change for the subject property from County MR to MR complies with
review criteria 3.

4) The ability of the subject property and surrounding vicinity to be developed according to the
Subdivision Standards in Article 4 considering the proposed zoning (UDC 2.2.1.d.4)
```

### Page 6 of 17

```text
UDC-21-00046

March 1, 2021

The subject property is not anticipated to be platted at this time as it is being used for access;
therefore, the subject property will not need to meet the standards of Article 4 at this time.
Should the lot be platted in the future, staff does not anticipate any issues with the subject
property meeting the standards of Article 4.

The proposed zone change for the subject property from County MR to MR complies with
review criteria 4.

5) The ability of the application to support the Intent and Applicability statements of the
proposed zoning district, and achieve the Design Objectives of any specific standards. (UDC
2.2.1.d.5)

The application supports the intent and applicability of the MR zone by providing access to City
infrastructure and public services.

The proposed zone change for the subject property from County MR to MR complies with
review criteria 5.

6) The ability of all potential future development to meet all applicable standards for
development in the proposed zoning district, including other development options in the
event that any specific development proposed in association with the application is not
executed after approval. (UDC 2.2.1.d.6)

The subject property is well suited to meet all applicable standards of the MR district should the
current proposed development not be executed. The MR zone will be cohesive with the
surrounding neighborhood.

The proposed zone change for the subject property from County MR to MR complies with
review criteria 6.

7) The review and recommendations of other reviewing bodies. (UDC 2.2.1.d.7)

The Planning and Development Department received the following review and
recommendations from other reviewing agencies:

•
Planning and Development
o Please remove the statement dedicating ROW. Corrected

The project was not sent out for review as it is a zone change accompanying an annexation that
was warranted by the conditions on the Conditional Use Approval, which was reviewed by all
typical reviewing agencies.

The proposed zone change for the subject property from County MR to MR complies with
review criteria 7.
